11. Important concepts for AI Platform Engineers
Concept	What it means
Schema validation	Checking whether incoming data follows a defined structure
Serialization	Converting Python data into a transferable format such as JSON
Deserialization	Converting incoming JSON into structured Python data
Custom validator	Your own validation rule
Nested model	A Pydantic model inside another model
Response model	Defines the structure of API output
Type annotation	Specifies the expected data type
How this applies to real AI platforms
Consider a production AI gateway that supports multiple providers.
It may need to validate:
•	Which AI model is requested.
•	Which provider owns that model.
•	Whether token limits are supported.
•	Whether streaming is enabled.
•	Whether the user has supplied valid generation parameters.
•	Whether metadata follows the expected structure.
Pydantic provides a strong foundation for these checks. Authentication, authorization, rate limits and provider-specific capabilities will be added in later stages.
12. Day 11 interview questions
Try answering these without looking at the explanations.
Q1. What is Pydantic, and why does FastAPI use it?
Pydantic validates and structures Python data using type annotations. FastAPI uses it to validate incoming request bodies and produce structured responses.
Q2. What is the difference between BaseModel and Field?
BaseModel creates the data model. Field adds constraints, defaults, descriptions and other field-level configuration.
Q3. What is a custom field validator?
It is a function that checks or transforms a field's value according to application-specific rules.
Q4. What is a nested Pydantic model?
It is a Pydantic model used as a field inside another model. It allows structured and reusable validation of complex JSON.
Q5. What is the difference between 400 and 422?
•	400: The request is understood but cannot be processed due to an application-level problem.
•	422: The request data fails validation.
Q6. What is response_model in FastAPI?
It specifies the expected response structure and allows FastAPI to validate and serialize the returned data.
Q7. What is the difference between str | None = None and str?
The first allows a string or None and is optional because it has a default. The second is a required string field.
